Hello Barbara,

To add to Heather's message yesterday: the search is finished and screening h=
as started. The search covered issued patents and published applications dire=
cted at the products Middleton, Sullivan and Wiley identified for clearance.

Screening runs in stages. Titles and abstracts come first, to set aside docum=
ents about unrelated technology. The independent claims of what remains are t=
hen read against your product description. Anything still in question gets a =
full reading of its claims and specification. What survives that last stage b=
ecomes the short list we chart. When the list is ready, we will propose a wor=
king session to take you through it before any charting starts.

The claim reading is done against the product description your team sent at t=
he start of the matter. If any feature has changed since then, please send th=
e current drawings or specification sheets now, so that each reading is done =
once and against the right design.

Nothing found so far is a conclusion about risk. Any view on a particular pat=
ent will come from Heather, in writing, after the claim review is complete.

